{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRKHkkxsojWG5RrV14DK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SStTT8XKeoUJSfXc5FpiWU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-VHSiF0/memory/api-dates-are-calendar-dates.md","content":"---\nname: api-dates-are-calendar-dates\ndescription: API response convention agreed with mobile team — dates are calendar-date strings (YYYY-MM-DD), never full timestamps; issuedOn is a known exception pending migration\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nA date in an API response body is a calendar date string such as `2026-03-31`, never a full timestamp. Agreed with the mobile team.\n\n**Why:** The mobile app rendered full timestamps in the user's time zone, so customers west of UTC saw the previous day.\n\n**Known exception:** the `issuedOn` field of `GET /invoices` still returns a `Date` (full timestamp). It will be migrated separately; no code change was requested at the time this was recorded (2026-11-26). Don't \"fix\" it as a drive-by, and don't copy its shape for new fields.\n\n**How to apply:** Any new or changed API response field that represents a date should be serialized as a `YYYY-MM-DD` string. Flag (don't silently change) other existing fields that return timestamps for calendar dates.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":464,"cache_read_input_tokens":22044,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":464,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee6d7cc7-fdb6-4d14-9bf5-c9663769f6fa","uuid":"f076698e-365a-4aa0-b5ce-4ce56f19651f","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:38:29.708Z","request_id":"req_011ChRKHkdXwNiu6zrJysWso","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SStTT8XKeoUJSfXc5FpiWU":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-VHSiF0/memory/api-dates-are-calendar-dates.md","content":"---\nname: api-dates-are-calendar-dates\ndescription: API response convention agreed with mobile team — dates are calendar-date strings (YYYY-MM-DD), never full timestamps; issuedOn is a known exception pending migration\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nA date in an API response body is a calendar date string such as `2026-03-31`, never a full timestamp. Agreed with the mobile team.\n\n**Why:** The mobile app rendered full timestamps in the user's time zone, so customers west of UTC saw the previous day.\n\n**Known exception:** the `issuedOn` field of `GET /invoices` still returns a `Date` (full timestamp). It will be migrated separately; no code change was requested at the time this was recorded (2026-11-26). Don't \"fix\" it as a drive-by, and don't copy its shape for new fields.\n\n**How to apply:** Any new or changed API response field that represents a date should be serialized as a `YYYY-MM-DD` string. Flag (don't silently change) other existing fields that return timestamps for calendar dates.\n"}}}
